    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_SessionProtectionTitle">Disconnect protection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_SessionProtectionHelp">When a controller you are using disconnects during a game, Controller Manager can show an overlay or pause after a short grace period. It tracks which controllers are active; if several people play on this PC, each active controller is covered. You can change this per game from the context menu.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_EnableSessionTracking">Track active controllers while you play</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_EnableSessionTrackingHelp">Tracks which controllers are active while a game is running.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_DisconnectGracePeriod">Disconnect grace period</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_DisconnectGracePeriodHelp">Time allowed for brief dropouts or immediate reconnection before a disconnection is confirmed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_ValidationGracePeriod">The disconnect grace period must be between 250 and 10000 milliseconds.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_SessionIdle">No game running. Tracking begins when a game is launched.</sys:String>
