    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_GamePolicyAllowTakeover">Single player. Allow play to continue with another controller</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_MenuSettings">Settings</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_ShowDisconnectOverlay">Show an overlay after a confirmed controller disconnection</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_ShowDisconnectOverlayHelp">The external overlay is informational and closes automatically when the incident is resolved or the game ends.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_DisconnectOverlayAppearanceHint">Turn the disconnect overlay on or off, and change how it looks, under</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_DisconnectOverlayAppearanceHintTrail">.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_ProtectAllActiveControllers">Use local multiplayer protection by default</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_ProtectAllActiveControllersHelp">Enable only when several local players use separate controllers. Automatic mode is recommended for single-player and online multiplayer games.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_GamePolicyLocalMultiplayer">Several players on this PC. Protect each player's controller</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_PauseGameOnDisconnect">Always suspend the game, regardless of network activity</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_PauseGameOnDisconnectHelp">Suspends the game process every time a controller disconnects, without checking for network activity. Works for all games regardless of input handling. The plugin never resumes the game automatically once the game ends.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="LOCCSM_PauseGameOnDisconnectWarning">Also suspends online matches; the plugin does not resume the game by itself.</sys:String>
